      formula: String.raw`\oint_{\gamma} f(z)\, dz = 2\pi i \sum_k \operatorname{Res}_{z_k} f`,
      text: "For a function f that is holomorphic on an open set containing a closed disc, except for finitely many isolated singularities z<sub>k</sub> inside the disc, the integral of f over the boundary circle γ is 2πi times the sum of the residues at the z<sub>k</sub>; Cauchy's integral formula is the special case of f(z)/(z − a). Added on 3 November 2026 as a premise of contour-integral proofs.",
      proof: "Goursat's lemma gives Cauchy's integral theorem for holomorphic functions on a disc. After subtracting the principal parts at the singularities, only the integrals of (z − z<sub>k</sub>)<sup>−m</sup> remain, which are 2πi for m = 1 and 0 otherwise. The proof rests on complex analysis, outside these graphs.",
      concepts: ["holomorphic-function"],
