      formula: String.raw`\Lambda(s, \chi) = \varepsilon(\chi)\, \Lambda(1 - s, \bar\chi)`,
      text: "For a primitive Dirichlet character χ modulo q > 1, L(s, χ) continues to an entire function, and Λ(s, χ) = (q/π)<sup>(s+a)/2</sup>Γ((s + a)/2)L(s, χ), with a ∈ {0, 1} the parity of χ, satisfies this functional equation with |ε(χ)| = 1.",
      proof: "As for ζ, Λ(s, χ) is the Mellin transform of the theta series twisted by χ; Poisson summation relates it to the theta series twisted by the conjugate character, with a Gauss sum as factor.",
      proofName: "Theta series twisted by χ",
      concepts: ["dirichlet-l-function", "dirichlet-character", "functional-equation"],
