      proof: "The Dirichlet series −ζ′(s)/ζ(s) of the von Mangoldt function has non-negative coefficients, and since ζ has no zeros on Re s = 1, it minus 1/(s − 1) is continuous on Re s ≥ 1; the Tauberian theorem gives ψ(x) ∼ x.",
